# Forge Block UI rules

Spec: @docs/design/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md (read the relevant sections before editing UI).
Reference images: `design/reference/matiks/` (home, menu-sheet, more-menu, insights, dialog, empty-state).
Data rules: `docs/design/data-availability.md`. Never show a value the bike or phone doesn't provide; label estimates "est.".

## Always
- Use tokens from `ui/theme/` (Color.kt, Type.kt, Shape.kt) via names; never `Color(0x…)`, literal radii or `fontSize =` in screen files. Missing token → add it to `ui/theme/` first.
- Build screens from `ui/components/` (ChunkyButton, ChunkyIconButton, BlockTile, SectionCard, IconTile, PillChip, DropdownLabel, StatPill, StatTriple, SectionLabel, ProgressPill, ChunkyDialog, EmptyState, ForgeTopBar, ForgeBottomNav). Missing component → create it there with a `@Preview` showing all states, then use it.
- Tappable = chunky (solid offset slab drawn with `drawBehind`, no `Modifier.shadow`) or a block/icon tile. Static content = flat.
- Text on pastel blocks is `OnBlock` (black). Lime only for selected / progress / go.
- Anton: UPPERCASE, ≥26sp, at most one display-size shout per screen. Everything else Nunito. Changing numbers use `tnum`.
- Block colours are semantic: Yellow = bike, Lavender = stats, Mint = guides/setup, Coral = ride/navigation. Max 4 blocks per screen.
- Replace stock `AlertDialog` with `ChunkyDialog`; empty lists get `EmptyState`.
- `HudColors.kt` names (`ForgeBlack`, `ForgeCard`, `SuzukiYellow`, `LabelMute`, …) are for `ui/hud/**` and `ui/sharecard/**` only. New portrait code never uses them. When restyling a screen, move it fully onto `Color.kt` tokens using the mapping table in spec §8.
- Portrait screens use `BumblebeeTheme`; the landscape HUD uses `HudTheme`. Don't swap them.
- Phase 2 (components) never edits screen files.

## Never
- Gradients, glows, blur shadows, Material Card elevation, outlined cards on portrait screens.
- White text on pastel blocks; Anton for body text.
- Copying Matiks artwork, mascots, icons or copy. Borrow the visual language only.
- Showing RPM, gear, engine/oil temp, battery voltage, throttle or fault codes.

## HUD and share-card exception
`ui/hud/**` and `ui/sharecard/**` keep the Forge cluster look (`design/hud-landscape/tokens.json`, HUD-only colours in `ui/theme/HudColors.kt`, Rajdhani numerals). No pastel blocks, illustrations or press animations there. Don't restyle these files unless the task explicitly says so.

## Workflow
- One screen per task, in the order of spec §5, following the `restyle-screen` skill (`.cursor/skills/restyle-screen/SKILL.md`).
- After changes, run `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` and fix errors before finishing.
- Finish by walking through the spec §9 checklist and reporting anything that doesn't pass.
